    <fr:title text="finite-field-invariants: a reference forest">finite-field-invariants: a reference forest</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>reference</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>This forest is the canonical statement layer of the
finite-field-invariants project: definitions, theorems, conjectures, and
the dependency skeleton that links them — kept separate from the
narrative journal (notes/steenrod-hsop.tex) and the experiment record
(experiments/). Notation is fixed here; when the journal and the forest
disagree, the forest wins and the journal gets patched.</html:p>
    <html:p>Each statement lives at a permanent numeric address. The number means
nothing and never changes: nodes are renamed, restated, split and
refuted, and the address survives all of it, so a citation written today
still resolves after the mathematics moves. The readable concordance is
ADDRESSES.md, regenerated by every build.</html:p>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-foundations/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-foundations</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-foundations/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="Foundations">Foundations</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>From the conjugation action to the statement of the height
  conjecture.</html:p>
        <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0001/" title="Setup: conjugation over a finite field" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0001/" display-uri="ffi-0001" type="local">The setup</fr:link> — the ambient objects, the conjugation
    action, and why it is modular.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0054/" title="The characteristic polynomial coefficients" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0054/" display-uri="ffi-0054" type="local">The characteristic polynomial coefficients</fr:link> — the
    <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> invariants the whole program takes as input.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0055/" title="The entrywise Frobenius" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0055/" display-uri="ffi-0055" type="local">The entrywise Frobenius</fr:link> — the direction everything
    deforms in.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0002/" title="The q-Steenrod operations" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0002/" display-uri="ffi-0002" type="local">The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[q]]></fr:tex>-Steenrod operations</fr:link> — the operations, and
    what they do to degrees.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0003/" title="The evaluation identity" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0003/" display-uri="ffi-0003" type="local">The evaluation identity</fr:link> — the one fact the program
    runs on.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0004/" title="Polarizations and the trace-form generators" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0004/" display-uri="ffi-0004" type="local">The polarizations</fr:link> — the sparse trace-form
    generators.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0005/" title="The Steenrod ideal" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/" display-uri="ffi-0005" type="local">The Steenrod ideal</fr:link> — the ideal whose height is in
    question.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0006/" title="The pencil criterion" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0006/" display-uri="ffi-0006" type="local">The pencil criterion</fr:link> — nilpotency to all orders in
    the Frobenius direction.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0007/" title="Flag witnesses for the partner variety" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0007/" display-uri="ffi-0007" type="local">The flag witnesses</fr:link> — the subvarieties that attain
    the lower bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0008/" title="The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0008/" display-uri="ffi-0008" type="local">The Krull bound</fr:link> — why the whole question is an upper
    bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">The height conjecture</fr:link> — the conjecture itself.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0010/" title="(*): the characteristic-p subvariety inference" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0010/" display-uri="ffi-0010" type="local">(*)</fr:link> — what is actually left to prove.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-symplectic/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-symplectic</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-symplectic/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="The symplectic skeleton">The symplectic skeleton</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>One idea at three scales. Avatar 1 is global, avatar 2 semi-local,
  avatar 3 infinitesimal; the thesis is that each is the same statement
  about half an orbit dimension.</html:p>
        <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0011/" title="The trace form" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0011/" display-uri="ffi-0011" type="local">The trace form</fr:link> — the pairing everything is measured
    in.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0012/" title="The three recurring numbers" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0012/" display-uri="ffi-0012" type="local">The three numbers</fr:link> — centralizer, orbit, and the
    half.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0013/" title="The thesis: every bound is half an orbit dimension" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0013/" display-uri="ffi-0013" type="local">The thesis</fr:link> — the thesis, and the three avatars.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0014/" title="Orbital varieties are Lagrangian" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0014/" display-uri="ffi-0014" type="local">Orbital varieties are Lagrangian</fr:link> — avatar 1,
    proven.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0015/" title="Nilpotent pencils, drop points, the centralizer sheaf" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0015/" display-uri="ffi-0015" type="local">The pencil apparatus</fr:link> — the semi-local apparatus.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0016/" title="(H1): the incidence theorem for flagless pencils" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0016/" display-uri="ffi-0016" type="local">(H1)</fr:link> — avatar 2, proven.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0049/" title="The germ apparatus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0049/" display-uri="ffi-0049" type="local">The germ apparatus</fr:link> — avatar 3, the germ apparatus.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0017/" title="Wall 1: coisotropy of the cyclic cocycle" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0017/" display-uri="ffi-0017" type="local">Wall 1</fr:link> — the bottom floor of the tower.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0051/" title="The anomaly law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0051/" display-uri="ffi-0051" type="local">The anomaly law</fr:link> — why characteristic 2.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-height/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-height</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-height/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="The height ladder">The height ladder</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>The conjecture is a theorem for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex>. Each rung is a
  different mechanism, and the reductions that carry rungs 8 and 9 are
  worth more than the rungs.</html:p>
        <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0018/" title="Height at n ≤ 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0018/" display-uri="ffi-0018" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  9]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the milestone.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0019/" title="Height at n ≤ 5" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0019/" display-uri="ffi-0019" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  5]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — finitely many orbits.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0020/" title="Height at n ≤ 7" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0020/" display-uri="ffi-0020" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n \le  7]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the modality theorem,
    unconditional.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0021/" title="(M8): the per-cell modality reduction at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0021/" display-uri="ffi-0021" type="local">(M8)</fr:link> — the address reduction at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0022/" title="Height at n = 8" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0022/" display-uri="ffi-0022" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 8]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — pseudo-Levi collapse and the
    torus defect.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0023/" title="(S): the n = 9 reduction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0023/" display-uri="ffi-0023" type="local">(S)</fr:link> — the reduction at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0024/" title="(S+): the ledger conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0024/" display-uri="ffi-0024" type="local">(S+)</fr:link> — the ledger that would close it.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0025/" title="Height at n = 9" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0025/" display-uri="ffi-0025" type="local">Height at <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 9]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the cascade.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-growth/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-growth</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-growth/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="The growth program">The growth program</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>Higman's class count, reached through the same Borel-orbit
  geometry. The chain from the definition of modality to the leading
  term of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\kappa (U_{n})]]></fr:tex> is complete except for one inequality, and the
  degree half of it is a theorem for every <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
        <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0026/" title="The class count kappa(U_n)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0026/" display-uri="ffi-0026" type="local">The class count</fr:link> — Higman's program.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0027/" title="Borel modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0027/" display-uri="ffi-0027" type="local">Borel modality</fr:link> — modality of the Borel on its
    nilradical.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0028/" title="U-modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0028/" display-uri="ffi-0028" type="local"><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex>-modality</fr:link> — modality of the unipotent
    group.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0029/" title="Theorem D: the modality cap" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0029/" display-uri="ffi-0029" type="local">Theorem D</fr:link> — the bridge to the class count.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0030/" title="z_u(c) and the modality formula" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0030/" display-uri="ffi-0030" type="local"><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[z_u(c)]]></fr:tex></fr:link> — the generic centralizer dimension.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0031/" title="The thread algebra" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0031/" display-uri="ffi-0031" type="local">The thread algebra</fr:link> — the algebra that computes it.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0032/" title="The graded count for z_u (H4)" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0032/" display-uri="ffi-0032" type="local">The graded count</fr:link> — the graded count and the defect.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0033/" title="(Deg-Opt): the grand formula for umod" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0033/" display-uri="ffi-0033" type="local">(Deg-Opt)</fr:link> — the closed form.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0034/" title="(P4): the maximum of umod over compositions" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0034/" display-uri="ffi-0034" type="local">(P4)</fr:link> — the maximum, and where it is attained.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0035/" title="(P5): the grand formula off the unimodal locus" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0035/" display-uri="ffi-0035" type="local">(P5)</fr:link> — the off-unimodal extension.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0036/" title="(P6): the collapse identity and the period-6 structure" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0036/" display-uri="ffi-0036" type="local">(P6)</fr:link> — the collapse identity and the origin of
    period 6.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0037/" title="The growth theorem" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0037/" display-uri="ffi-0037" type="local">The growth theorem</fr:link> — the unconditional lower bound.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0038/" title="The degree law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0038/" display-uri="ffi-0038" type="local">The degree law</fr:link> — the degree.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0039/" title="The leading-term law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0039/" display-uri="ffi-0039" type="local">The leading-term law</fr:link> — the leading coefficient.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0040/" title="The M-law: the unimodal side of the leading-term law" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0040/" display-uri="ffi-0040" type="local">The M-law</fr:link> — its proven half.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0041/" title="(TOP-X): rigidity of maximal modality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0041/" display-uri="ffi-0041" type="local">(TOP-X)</fr:link> — the rigidity statement it needs.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-frontier/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-frontier</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-frontier/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="The frontier">The frontier</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>Two live fronts. The (NS) chain is the sole residue of the growth
  program; the germ-scale front is where the wall program ran out, and
  is kept on the record because what it refuted is load-bearing.</html:p>
        <html:ul><html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0042/" title="Splits, flanks, tallness" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0042/" display-uri="ffi-0042" type="local">Splits and tallness</fr:link> — splits, flanks, tallness.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0043/" title="Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0043/" display-uri="ffi-0043" type="local">Lemma V</fr:link> — false as stated.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0044/" title="Tall-Lemma V" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0044/" display-uri="ffi-0044" type="local">Tall-Lemma V</fr:link> — true where it matters.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0045/" title="(NS): the strict/centralizer inequality" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0045/" display-uri="ffi-0045" type="local">(NS)</fr:link> — the open inequality.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0046/" title="The Fredholm ledger" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0046/" display-uri="ffi-0046" type="local">The Fredholm ledger</fr:link> — the exact ledger.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0047/" title="(Q-MOD): the reductive repair" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0047/" display-uri="ffi-0047" type="local">(Q-MOD)</fr:link> — the first reduction.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0048/" title="The peeling induction" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0048/" display-uri="ffi-0048" type="local">The peeling induction</fr:link> — the second reduction.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0050/" title="(W): the wall conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0050/" display-uri="ffi-0050" type="local">(W)</fr:link> — refuted from <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n = 6]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0052/" title="(L2): decreasing monomial germs are vacuous" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0052/" display-uri="ffi-0052" type="local">(L2)</fr:link> — proven.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0053/" title="(L3): the vacuity family" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0053/" display-uri="ffi-0053" type="local">(L3)</fr:link> — refuted, and productive.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-notation/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-notation</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-notation/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="Notation">Notation</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>The notation layer is a node like any other: it is where every
  symbol in the forest is defined, and it is the only place a macro may
  be introduced. Read <fr:link href="/ffi/preamble/" title="Forest preamble: the notation layer" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/preamble/" display-uri="preamble" type="local">Forest preamble: the notation layer</fr:link> for the index of the seven notation
  nodes, the mechanics of forester's
  <html:code><![CDATA[\def]]></html:code>, and the list of glyphs that
  currently carry two meanings.</html:p>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors />
        <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/sec-conventions/</fr:uri>
        <fr:display-uri>sec-conventions</fr:display-uri>
        <fr:route>/ffi/sec-conventions/</fr:route>
        <fr:title text="Conventions">Conventions</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p><html:strong>Addresses.</html:strong> Statement nodes are <html:code>ffi-NNNN</html:code>, assigned
  in order of minting and never reassigned. Infrastructure —
  <fr:link href="/ffi/preamble/" title="Forest preamble: the notation layer" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/preamble/" display-uri="preamble" type="local">Forest preamble: the notation layer</fr:link>, the seven <html:code>macros-</html:code> nodes, this index — keeps
  readable addresses, because it is named after what it is rather than
  after a claim that might be restated.</html:p>
        <html:p><html:strong>Taxon and tags.</html:strong> The taxon is the grammatical kind:
  definition, theorem, proposition, lemma, corollary, conjecture,
  principle, notation, reference. Tags carry area — foundations,
  symplectic, height, growth, frontier — and status: proven, open,
  conditional, refuted. A node tagged refuted is still a node; it is on
  the record because the refutation is a result.</html:p>
        <html:p><html:strong>One claim per node.</html:strong> If a node states two things, it is two
  nodes. This is why the address space is sparse rather than
  hierarchical: splitting a node mints new addresses and leaves the old
  one in place, pointing forward.</html:p>
        <html:p><html:strong>Dependencies.</html:strong> Every node carries
  <html:code><![CDATA[\import{preamble}]]></html:code> for notation and
  nothing else; each mathematical dependency is a link in the
  <html:code><![CDATA[\uses{...}]]></html:code> line, because forester derives
  its backlink graph from links and not from imports. Until proof nodes
  exist, that line carries what a proof's inline citations would.
  <html:code>./check-dag.py</html:code> verifies that every link resolves, that the
  graph is acyclic, and that nothing is stranded.</html:p>
        <html:p><html:strong>Provenance.</html:strong> Every statement node ends with a line pointing
  into the journal and the experiment record. Full proofs live in the
  journal; proof nodes are a later pass.</html:p>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
